{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>A man of understanding</b> — Scripture does not mention him. Perhaps he is Sherebiah, mentioned in the verse, and the vav is added like the vav in ואיה וענה, or it is a vav added to the sense, and he did not wish to mention him twice. Thus the interpretation is: \"a man of understanding, Sherebiah,\" and Sherebiah and his sons and his brothers were eighteen — and this is correct."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The verse citation 'mentioned in the verse' likely refers to Ezra 8:24 or the list in vv. 18–19 where Sherebiah appears; no specific citation is given in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:17.195795668Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}